WEBVTT

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:02.600
Margrave Guize.

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.660
You have my gratitude and respect 
for continuing to fight,

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:08.320
single-handedly, for the sake of the kingdom.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.100
But the Kingdom of Soleil is 
now in a difficult position.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.370
Our capital city, Hariant, 
is currently occupied.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:22.120
We do not wish to see any more 
pointless losses or deaths.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.290
<i>Not only did you get yourself captured,</i>

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:27.040
<i>now you're acting as the Empire's lapdog?</i>

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.560
<i>I'm disappointed.</i>

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:30.340
<i>Have you lost your pride?</i>

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:35.330
<i>It has been a month since the princess 
abandoned her people and fled.</i>

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.610
<i>No matter how young she may be,</i>

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:39.760
<i>she should have comported herself in 
a manner more appropriate to her station.</i>

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:42.240
Margrave. The princess has not abandoned—

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.020
<i>No excuses!</i>

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:50.110
<i>My pride demands that I defend
my ancestral lands to the end.</i>

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.280
<i>Excuse me.</i>

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.430
Commander Eine is here to see you.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:19.130
The Price of Smiles

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:19.130
<i>The Price of Smiles</i>

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:39.430
<b><i>The Sunflowers of the Palace</i></b>

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:46.640
There was a lot of shelling 
in this area, too, huh?

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:49.460
It's a strange feeling...

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:52.030
seeing the aftermath of our attacks on them.

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:55.100
And vice-versa, too.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:59.290
Yeah... looking at Pierce since he got hurt.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:02.160
It's still hard for me.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:03.510
Yes.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:07.300
Especially since he's trying 
so hard to be strong...

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:14.070
I thought this was the royal palace.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:16.370
Yeah, pathetic.

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:17.880
Hey, how'd it go?

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:20.680
This should be our last visit 
to Pierce in the hospital.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:22.620
What, is he finally kicking the bucket?

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:25.570
You idiot. He's being 
discharged this evening.

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:26.640
Today?

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:30.030
So Stella and I were talking, and...

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:34.150
I was wondering if we could 
all send Pierce off together.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:39.410
So the western Margrave 
won't submit that easily?

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:42.910
Though they're technically part of our domain, 
it is a region with much history.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:46.120
You can force me to advocate on your behalf,

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.750
but that doesn't mean they'll listen.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:50.310
I'm aware of the difficulty.

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:52.760
Try your hardest to 
convince them, regardless.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:56.250
Neither of us wants to see more 
pointless bloodshed, do we?

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:57.920
Pointless blood?

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:02.820
Don't you mean, "I'd rather not have 
to divide my forces, if possible"?

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:08.900
I anticipated that the 
Royal Senate would flee here.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:12.080
I'd naïvely assumed that their 
surrender would come soon after...

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:13.940
I didn't expect they would 
give us this much trouble.

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:17.460
Rumors say that

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:21.200
it's the runaway princess who commands 
the remaining resistance. Is it true?

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:22.840
I wouldn't know.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:25.520
I've been a bird in a cage for over a month.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.280
I'm in no position to hear such things.

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:33.960
Then, as a bird in a cage, do keep singing...

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.840
The song, "surrender to the Empire."

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:40.710
A farewell party, eh?

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:42.040
Sounds fine.

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:44.390
You can use my room if you'd like.

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:45.920
Thank you, sir.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:49.880
But there's no decent food 
to have a proper feast.

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:52.490
Seems a little late for the buddy-buddy act.

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:55.030
Why do you always have to be this way?

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:57.600
There you are, Huey! And company.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:58.750
Guy?

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:00.050
What're you doing here?

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:02.610
What do you think? I'm joining you guys!

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.160
Who's that guy again?

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:06.880
From the fight on the River Deese...

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:10.740
Remember the sad fool who was 
all like "ahh, they got us"?

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.890
Oh, I remember now!

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:14.830
Don't exaggerate.

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:17.530
But, what do you mean, you're joining us?

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:19.500
The decision was made unofficially.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:21.800
He's filling in for Pierce.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:24.360
I look forward to serving with you!

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:25.420
You heard the man.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:28.550
I even brought a present.

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:31.270
From my private stash.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:33.130
Don't spare the gratitude, okay?

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:34.430
You drank half.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.690
What if we all brought food?

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:41.400
What are you talking about?

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.340
Of course! That's a great idea!

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:47.230
Let's all bring things 
from our private stores!

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:49.030
Seriously, what are you talking about?!

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.620
My Emperor.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:54.650
I've received word that the 
information Advisor Langford gave us

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:56.910
has nearly been decoded.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:58.360
<i>I see.</i>

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:02.060
<i>Does that mean we'll be able to mass-produce</i>

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:04.200
<i>the new chrars currently in our possession?</i>

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:06.820
Yes, almost certainly.

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:08.370
However...

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:09.430
<i>Yes?</i>

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:12.800
With the end of the conflict in sight,

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:16.700
hasn't the need for mass 
production become less urgent?

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:20.820
As you know, the new chrars are 
rife with issues, and given—

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:21.830
<i>Enough.</i>

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:25.550
<i>Soldiers die under my flag.</i>

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:29.100
<i>When your crest represents 
no tradition, no bloodline,</i>

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:34.330
<i>the only way it can command 
loyalty is with power.</i>

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:37.380
<i>I know that better than anyone.</i>

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:41.960
I'm pretty sure...

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:49.590
It probably won't be enough.

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:51.140
Even if we all bring some...

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:54.570
Is something wrong?

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:56.520
This smell...

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:03.560
Totally not enough.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:06.170
Some party this is gonna be.

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:07.830
You're one to talk.

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:10.180
You didn't even bring anything!

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:13.060
Open up! Please open the door!

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.200
I thought we could share this.

00:07:17.690 --> 00:07:18.610
What's all this?

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:23.960
Apparently some stray fire hit the palace 
wine cellar and blew a hole in it.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:28.180
Most of the wine was ruined, 
and they were going to throw it out.

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:29.470
So you took some?

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:31.770
Stella is amazing!

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:34.940
She picked up the smell of 
the spilled wine right away!

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:39.730
Well... I have a memory of playing 
around in a place like that long ago.

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:42.930
You came from a household with a wine cellar?

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:44.980
Or maybe it was in the neighborhood...

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:47.250
It was a really long time ago.

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:49.720
The memories are fuzzy.

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:51.860
Get outta the way!

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:53.950
Potatoes?

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:58.420
The load was starting to go bad, and they 
were desperate for a way to get rid of them.

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:01.280
But they don't seem to be 
in terrible condition...

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.910
Well, you stay in the military long enough,

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:07.140
you pick up a loyal squadmate or two.

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:09.170
Sounds like I'm up, then.

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:11.270
Is the kitchen free?

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:17.180
How shocking!

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:20.650
I didn't know Huey had such skills.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:22.690
What?

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:29.960
Okay, enough peeling.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:31.860
Break, go cook those sardines.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:33.520
Huh? But they're canned!

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:35.320
So grill 'em in the can.

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:38.580
A little extra effort goes a long way.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:40.680
Wh-Which one's the grill?

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:43.610
Quiet down! Someone's gonna come!

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:44.340
You people!

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:47.270
Cooking isn't something you can do quietly!

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:49.960
And you, quit staring and put 
those potatoes in the mixer!

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:52.280
You don't have to be so bossy!

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:53.090
What should I do?

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:54.610
Let's see...

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:55.930
Here, chateau these.

00:08:56.770 --> 00:08:57.430
Huh?

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:59.430
Okay. Then trim these.

00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:02.060
"Trim"?

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:03.350
Forget it!

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:05.430
Go decorate the room or something.

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:12.820
How beautiful!

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:15.400
They're artificial, of course.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:23.230
You think she came from a 
fancy household, after all?

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:25.710
I've never thought to ask,

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:28.790
and she doesn't seem to 
want to talk about it...

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:49.080
I feel weirdly nervous.

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:51.320
Let's skip the pleasantries.

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:53.530
To Pierce's release from the hospital.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:54.740
Cheers!

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.530
Cheers!

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:01.980
Amazing. You did all this...

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:03.660
Of course, it's almost all potatoes.

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:05.910
But we worked hard to make it.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:07.920
Huey and all of us.

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:13.630
W-Wow. It's so good! 
Really, really good!

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:18.510
How to put it... it's rich, but not cloying.

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:20.490
This is delicious!

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:22.560
I know. This is perfect.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:25.210
I've been carrying these around with me.

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:27.890
Would you like to try some?

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:29.430
What are they?

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:30.710
Bugsy beans.

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:32.400
They're a local delicacy from my hometown.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.220
They're an acquired taste,

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:36.340
but they can be quite addictive 
once you're used to them.

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:38.400
Would you like to try one, Commander?

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:41.030
I'm not really a fan of beans...

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:42.980
They look delicious!

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:47.130
Wait. Hang on, I've heard of these beans.

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:51.240
When we feed these to Royal Army 
POWs, they complain about torture!

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:55.130
Wh-What the hell is this?!

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:58.760
W-Well... that's a local delicacy for you.

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:02.490
They're rather... unique.

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:03.260
They're gross!

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:05.210
Hey, you guys okay?

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.230
You don't have to force it...

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.750
Water! I need water!

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:10.600
Wait!

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:12.100
If you want to kill the taste, try this.

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:15.130
It's what we drink in my hometown 
after you eat something gross.

00:11:15.130 --> 00:11:15.820
You see...

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:21.930
It's even more gross, which cancels it out!

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:22.950
You ass!

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:24.740
You just doubled the grossness!

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:24.740
That's strange...

00:11:26.020 --> 00:11:29.000
I told you, you don't need to force it...

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:35.020
Don't worry. I'll be filling 
your shoes and then some.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:37.050
Head on home without a care.

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:38.230
Hey.

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:41.510
But it'll be nice to be home, huh?

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:42.420
I guess.

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:43.730
You guess?

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:46.630
It never feels nice to get let go.

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:48.760
He's getting a discharge 
for injury, remember?

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:52.770
Still, your family'll be happy to see you.

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:56.230
I'm afraid I was a burden 
to them from the start.

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:58.920
You know the saying... 
"poor farmers, big families."

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:02.660
I basically joined the military 
to be one less mouth to feed.

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:07.030
A long time ago, someone tricked my father

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:11.040
into buying a large shipment of 
crop seeds that wouldn't root.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:15.530
He lost a fortune, and our family 
spiraled from there into poverty.

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:16.830
What the hell?

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:18.920
Don't any of us come from a not-terrible life?

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:20.310
What'll you do next?

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:22.420
Got a job lined up?

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:25.500
Well... I haven't really decided.

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:28.680
Would you like to work at my orphanage, then?

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:33.060
Commander, what did you...

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:37.440
I run an orphanage. I was asking 
if you'd like to help out there.

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:39.470
Why do you run an orphanage?

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:41.110
Do I need a reason?

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:42.950
No...

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:45.200
What do you think?

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:46.790
Well...

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:48.220
Is that a no?

00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:49.200
No...

00:12:49.430 --> 00:12:53.100
Well, it's just so sudden...

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:55.210
Think about it, then.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:56.300
Let me know before you go.

00:13:06.710 --> 00:13:07.760
Excuse me.

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:14.590
I'm sure you were told to investigate 
if you saw me writing anything down.

00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:16.500
They're baby names.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:17.840
Baby names?

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:20.960
My next will be born soon.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:24.360
But I'm having trouble 
thinking up good names...

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:28.240
Excuse me, sir.

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:31.880
Warrant Officer Break and Huey 
went back to their rooms.

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:33.420
Guy, too?

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:34.450
Yes.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:38.080
He was stumbling drunk, so the Warrant 
Officer took him back to his room...

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:41.060
Lily took a walk to settle her stomach.

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:42.960
She ate too much, she said.

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:45.820
I see. You sleep, too.

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:47.810
We can clean this all up tomorrow.

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:48.890
Yes, sir.

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:51.970
Ah... Where's Pierce?

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:54.030
He left a little while ago.

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:56.830
What did he say?

00:13:57.700 --> 00:13:59.110
About the orphanage?

00:13:59.710 --> 00:14:01.700
He hasn't made up his mind yet.

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:04.360
I thought it was a wonderful offer, myself.

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:07.790
I'm not sure I'd say an 
orphanage is wonderful.

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:11.070
But I thought he might appreciate it.

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:16.250
He said his father once told him...

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:19.710
"You're a crop that won't root, too."

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:24.230
Apparently he was a bit of a troublemaker.

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:26.660
Well, it's a common story for young people,

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:29.430
at that age before they've 
figured themselves out.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:33.140
But, apparently, those words 
cut him pretty deep.

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:37.390
"They say I'm like the crops that 
brought my family to ruin"...

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:43.610
"How could someone like me 
ever look after children?"

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:46.570
I think he'll be fine.

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:53.980
Those who know pain are better 
equipped to understand the feelings

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:57.490
of children who have suffered.

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:01.290
Were you one of those children, too?

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:10.550
Come here! Call me Mom!

00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:17.580
I told you it's not working!

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:19.800
It's not working...

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:22.380
I don't even know if I'll 
be able to keep my job.

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:24.730
I don't know if we'll be able to feed her...

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:27.230
But you were so happy when she was born!

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:29.110
But things have changed since then!

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.630
If only we hadn't taken that girl in...

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:44.470
Are you saying it's not good enough for you?

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:47.880
Then wipe that expression off your face.

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:54.480
That's right.

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:56.730
Just keep smiling.

00:15:57.160 --> 00:16:00.640
Smiling will get you through anything.

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:35.200
The children I'm trying to raise

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:38.280
probably aren't the kind 
you're thinking about.

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:42.840
I don't want to raise weak children

00:16:42.840 --> 00:16:46.310
who rely on commiseration 
to fumble through life.

00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:52.070
Nor children who lie to themselves and 
smile just to placate those around them.

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:59.950
Pierce is just looking for reasons to 
justify his lack of self-confidence.

00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:05.250
It's not the flower that decides it 
won't root, it's the people around it.

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:07.340
Flowers and crops both...

00:17:08.070 --> 00:17:11.330
They fight with all they have to take 
root and survive, don't you think?

00:17:13.810 --> 00:17:15.260
I'll go to bed, too.

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:16.650
Haven't been this drunk in a while.

00:17:28.470 --> 00:17:29.590
Stella!

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:33.070
Lily. And Pierce...

00:17:33.430 --> 00:17:35.270
I ran into him before.

00:17:35.270 --> 00:17:37.110
He made me this weird proposal...

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:38.760
Well...

00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:42.120
Please don't say it that way. 
She'll get the wrong idea.

00:17:42.610 --> 00:17:46.740
It's just... this may be a silly 
request from a country bumpkin,

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:50.000
but I'd like to see the royal palace...

00:17:50.280 --> 00:17:51.550
The royal palace?

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:52.680
But we're technically in...

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:54.740
Oh, we know that.

00:17:54.740 --> 00:17:56.010
But, look!

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:58.370
The places the royals actually lived...

00:17:58.370 --> 00:18:01.140
We rank-and-file aren't 
allowed in without leave.

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:02.730
If I have to return to the country,

00:18:02.730 --> 00:18:05.020
I'd like to bring a good story back with me.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:06.960
Want to come, Stella?

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:09.430
I'd like to see it myself.

00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:14.650
Stop.

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:16.030
That way!

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:18.460
Hide!

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:33.090
Smiling will get you through anything.

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:36.670
Nor children who lie to themselves and 
smile just to placate those around them.

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:44.460
Amazing...

00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:46.040
Yeah, it's amazing.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:48.100
Thanks.

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:50.550
This will make a great 
story to take back home.

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:51.940
Are we done here, then?

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:55.750
Seeing as we've come this far, 
why not venture further?

00:18:57.890 --> 00:19:00.520
A greenhouse... in a place like this?

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:04.330
It's so beautiful!

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:10.960
I've never seen flowers like these before.

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:13.460
Are they dead?

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:16.960
Flowers that didn't root?

00:19:19.490 --> 00:19:22.590
But look, they've grown this big.

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:26.570
Even if it's hard for them to grow,

00:19:26.570 --> 00:19:29.600
they still did so, 
while someone cared for them.

00:19:30.970 --> 00:19:34.610
You're right. They might not have had to die.

00:19:36.420 --> 00:19:38.740
Someone took really good care of them.

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:43.490
Someone came and went, 
giving them water and love...

00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:47.990
"It's not the flower that 
decides it won't root."

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:50.460
"It's the people around it 
who are convinced that it won't."

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:53.630
The commander told me that.

00:19:54.180 --> 00:19:55.940
"Flowers and crops both..."

00:19:55.940 --> 00:19:58.630
"They fight with all they have 
to take root and survive."

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:05.690
You think the commander's asleep already?

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:07.390
Most likely.

00:20:08.510 --> 00:20:12.650
But he's probably waiting to hear from you.

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:22.290
<i>Who put so much love and care into 
raising these flowers, and why?</i>

00:20:29.480 --> 00:20:32.240
You'll be home soon?

00:20:32.240 --> 00:20:33.040
Yeah.

00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:36.550
The border will soon be in sight.

00:20:36.550 --> 00:20:37.940
Then it's just a little bit longer...

00:20:46.420 --> 00:20:47.510
That can't be true!

00:20:48.190 --> 00:20:52.770
The transport hover Pierce was in
 was attacked near the border.

00:20:53.760 --> 00:20:54.770
Any survivors?

00:20:59.220 --> 00:21:00.130
But...

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:04.970
He was going to stop back home, 
then go to your orphanage...

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:07.130
He seemed so happy...

00:21:07.650 --> 00:21:08.530
It's so...

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:10.540
It's so...

00:21:16.010 --> 00:21:18.820
But that's reality for you, isn't it?

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:22.630
When a pathetic fool starts to dream,

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:24.520
he's just setting himself up for a fall.

00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:25.180
Huey...

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:39.030
At times like these, you can't 
do much but smile. Right?

00:23:35.100 --> 00:23:40.350
<b><i>The Final Message</i></b>
